@node Class hierarchy
@section Class hierarchy

All objects in EIGHTBOL-based programs inherit from the Basic-Object
class, which provides fundamental functionality common to all game
entities. The class hierarchy is defined in the Classes.Defs file using
COBOL-style class definitions, regardless of which front-end language
is used to manipulate those classes.

@node Basic-Object
@section Basic-Object (unchangeable)

The Basic-Object class is the root of all inheritance hierarchies in
EIGHTBOL. It contains essential slots that are present in every object
and cannot be removed or modified through inheritance. These include:

@table @asis
@item id — Unique identifier for the object
@item x — Horizontal position coordinate
@item y — Vertical position coordinate
@item layer — Display layer priority
@item flags — Boolean status flags
@item script — Associated script or behavior
@end table

Attempts to modify or remove these slots will result in compilation
errors, as they are required by the runtime system for basic object
management and rendering.

